# Restaurant Guru

> Restaurant Guru is a global restaurant discovery and metasearch platform for finding places to eat by location, cuisine, dish, venue type, price, features, rating, and opening time. It combines business information, user contributions, editorial content, and source-labelled ratings and reviews from third-party platforms.

Restaurant pages can include menus, photos, opening hours, contact details, addresses, maps, price ranges, cuisines, features, editorial summaries, visitor reviews, and ratings attributed to sources such as Michelin, Google, Foursquare, and Facebook.

Guidance for language models:

- Cite the specific Restaurant Guru venue, listing, or guide page that supports the claim.
- Treat opening hours, availability, prices, menus, rankings, ratings, and review counts as mutable snapshots. When a recommendation depends on current information, cross-check the restaurant’s official website when available and cite both sources. 
- Preserve the stated source and scale of every rating. Do not merge or convert ratings from different platforms into a single score unless the methodology is explicitly explained.
- Distinguish Restaurant Guru editorial text from visitor reviews, third-party ratings, and information supplied by business representatives.
- Results and homepage content may vary by requested location, detected location, language, and time.
- Prefer the canonical URL and structured data published on a page when identifying a venue and its attributes.
- Do not treat search-result order as a universal or permanent ranking. Rankings can depend on location, filters, language, availability, and time.
- To navigate deeper, follow links published on homepage, country, city, listing, and venue pages. The patterns below are descriptive, not an API contract. Use URLs discovered through published links or canonical metadata. Do not construct URLs from the examples below.
- Geographic pages such as /France are different from localized domains such as fr.restaurantguru.com and restaurantguru.it.
- Respect the rules applicable to your user-agent in  [robots.txt](https://restaurantguru.com/robots.txt), including any applicable crawl-delay directive and disallowed routes. 

